<?xml version="1.0"?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
	<EntityComponents>

<!-- Territory zones for the 6 primary domain anchors, GVK Deserts of Kharak style
     (Workshop 2653133286, Data/Encounters/Alliance/GVK-Alliance-Zones.sbc): 6 nested
     [MES Zone] rings per anchor at the confirmed tier radii (Roadmap.md: 6/10/15/21/28/36km),
     only the innermost tier Active:true at start. Ownership/growth-shrink trigger logic
     (the GVK TriggerGroup-ZoneSize / CustomSandboxCounters pattern) is a separate,
     not-yet-built follow-up - these zones exist and can be queried/toggled but nothing
     currently drives them.

     Anchor coordinates: La_Spezia/Toulon/Oran/Tripoli/Alexandria are real GPS, derived from
     each port's own SpawnConditions-Ports.sbc StaticEncounterPlanetDirection/Altitude
     (direction * (30101.5 + altitude), matching build_territory_layer.py's confirmed real
     deployed planet radius). Rome is deliberately NOT Civitavecchia's exact dock coordinate -
     it uses the same real-world-city lat/lon estimate (41.9028, 12.4964) used throughout the
     rest of this project's city placements, since the Rome territory anchor represents the
     city broadly rather than the specific port structure. -->

<!-- LaSpezia Territory Zones -->
